# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repository-controlled line endings. Two independent reasons this file exists:
#
# 1. MIGRATION CHECKSUMS (original rule, below). Migration checksums are computed
#    over RAW FILE BYTES (see backend/app/migrations.py: discover_migrations ->
#    hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes())), and those checksums are persisted in
#    schema_migrations and compared on every subsequent run. Line endings must
#    therefore be byte-identical on every platform.
#
#    Without this, core.autocrlf=true smudges LF -> CRLF on Windows checkout, so a
#    database migrated on Windows records different checksums than the same commit
#    checked out on Linux/CI/containers. The next run from the other platform sees
#    checksum drift on every applied migration and refuses to apply anything.
#
# 2. EVIDENCE-BOUND PROOF FILES. The accepted restricted-PostgreSQL runtime
#    manifest freezes a SHA-256 per accepted child guard, and tenant-authorization
#    evidence v3 binds the SHA-256 of every accepted proof implementation. Those
#    digests are computed over raw file bytes too, so under core.autocrlf=true a
#    fresh checkout materializes CRLF and the digests legitimately fail closed --
#    which made evidence unreproducible outside one developer working tree.
#
#    Pinning eol=lf for the source formats makes checkout materialization
#    byte-identical to the committed blob on every platform and for any value of
#    core.autocrlf, so accepted proofs and evidence verify from a pristine
#    checkout. No repository content changes: every tracked blob is already LF.
#
# Binary formats are explicitly marked -text so they can never be smudged.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- migrations (original rule; byte-stable checksums) ---
*.sql text eol=lf

# --- source formats bound by accepted proof / evidence digests ---
*.py   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.tsx  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf

# --- binary formats: never treat as text, never smudge ---
*.pdf   -text
*.png   -text
*.jpg   -text
*.jpeg  -text
*.webp  -text
*.gif   -text
*.ico   -text
*.zip   -text
*.gz    -text
*.woff  -text
*.woff2 -text
*.xlsx  -text
*.docx  -text

# No intentional CRLF fixture exists in this repository: at the commit that
# introduced this policy, zero tracked blobs contained CRLF, so pinning eol=lf
# cannot alter any fixture's meaning. Should a CRLF-significant fixture ever be
# added, give it an explicit path rule here (e.g. `path/to/fixture.txt -text`)
# and state why, rather than relaxing the rules above.
